{% comment %}
  One row of low-inventory-threshold-config, matched against the current product.

  Input:  threshold_handle   product handle or SKU. A '*' at either end drops the
                             anchor on that side:

                               'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN'         the whole value
                               'late-night-crackers-*'  starts with
                               '*-en-pack'              ends with
                               '*late-night-crackers*'  contains, anywhere

                             Blank ignores the row, as does a bare '*', which
                             would otherwise claim every product in the store.
          threshold_maximum  highest count that still prints a notice, or 'all'
                             for every count. Anything else ignores the row.

  From low-inventory-threshold.liquid: low_inventory_threshold_keys, the current
  product's identifiers, each wrapped in pipes. The pipes are what the anchors
  are made of: a whole-value row is compared with both, so 'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN'
  cannot claim 'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN-PACK'; a starts-with row keeps the opening pipe,
  so 'crackers-*' cannot claim 'late-night-crackers-ep3'; a contains row keeps
  neither and matches anywhere inside an identifier.

  Output is left in low_inventory_threshold, low_inventory_threshold_all and
  low_inventory_threshold_matched. The first matching row wins: once a row has
  matched, the rows after it are skipped.

  The inputs are cleared again at the end. `include` shares the caller's scope on
  EasyStore, so a row that omits a value would otherwise inherit the previous
  row's.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_handle = threshold_handle | default: '' | append: '' | strip | downcase %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_value = threshold_maximum | default: '' | append: '' | strip | downcase %}
{% comment %}
  A '*' at the start or the end is stripped and remembered as a dropped anchor.
  Only those two positions mean anything: a '*' left in the middle can never
  appear in a handle or a SKU, so the row is ignored rather than kept as one that
  silently matches nothing.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_start = '|' %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_end = '|' %}
{% comment %}
  The value with every '*' removed is rebuilt into the three wildcard shapes and
  compared with what was written. A row that matches none of them put its '*'
  somewhere that means nothing - in the middle, where no handle or SKU can have
  one - and is dropped, rather than kept as a row that silently matches nothing.

  Rebuilding rather than reading the ends keeps this to `replace` and a string
  comparison. `slice` would say the same thing in fewer lines, but nothing else
  in this theme uses it, and this snippet has to run on EasyStore's Liquid rather
  than the one the tests use.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_core = low_inventory_threshold_row_handle | replace: '*', '' %}
{% if low_inventory_threshold_row_core != low_inventory_threshold_row_handle %}
  {% capture low_inventory_threshold_row_contains %}*{{ low_inventory_threshold_row_core }}*{% endcapture %}
  {% capture low_inventory_threshold_row_ends_with %}*{{ low_inventory_threshold_row_core }}{% endcapture %}
  {% capture low_inventory_threshold_row_starts_with %}{{ low_inventory_threshold_row_core }}*{% endcapture %}
  {% if low_inventory_threshold_row_handle == low_inventory_threshold_row_contains %}
    {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_start = '' %}
    {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_end = '' %}
  {% elsif low_inventory_threshold_row_handle == low_inventory_threshold_row_ends_with %}
    {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_start = '' %}
  {% elsif low_inventory_threshold_row_handle == low_inventory_threshold_row_starts_with %}
    {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_end = '' %}
  {% else %}
    {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_core = '' %}
  {% endif %}
  {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_handle = low_inventory_threshold_row_core %}
{% endif %}
{% unless low_inventory_threshold_matched %}
  {% if low_inventory_threshold_row_handle != '' and low_inventory_threshold_row_value != '' %}
    {% capture low_inventory_threshold_row_key %}{{ low_inventory_threshold_row_start }}{{ low_inventory_threshold_row_handle }}{{ low_inventory_threshold_row_end }}{% endcapture %}
    {% if low_inventory_threshold_keys contains low_inventory_threshold_row_key %}
      {% if low_inventory_threshold_row_value == 'all' %}
        {% assign low_inventory_threshold_all = true %}
        {% assign low_inventory_threshold_matched = true %}
      {% else %}
        {% comment %} A non-numeric maximum reads as 0 and is ignored, so a typo leaves the product on the default instead of silently hiding its notice. {% endcomment %}
        {% assign low_inventory_threshold_row_number = low_inventory_threshold_row_value | plus: 0 %}
        {% if low_inventory_threshold_row_number > 0 %}
          {% assign low_inventory_threshold = low_inventory_threshold_row_number %}
          {% assign low_inventory_threshold_matched = true %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endunless %}
{% assign threshold_handle = '' %}
{% assign threshold_maximum = '' %}
